{"name":"White Chocolate","hex":"#f0e3c7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white chocolate","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food made from cocoa butter, milk, and sugar, having no cocoa solids.","A piece of confectionery consisting of this."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white_chocolate"}],"entries":[{"title":"White chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"White chocolate is chocolate made from cocoa butter, sugar, and milk solids. It is ivory in color and lacks the dark appearance of most other types of chocolate because it does not contain the non-fat solid components of cocoa. Due to this omission, as well as its sweetness and the occasional use of additives, some consumers do not consider white chocolate to be real chocolate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Chopped_white_chocolate_chunks.jpg/330px-Chopped_white_chocolate_chunks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_chocolate"},{"title":"Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate is a food made from roasted and ground cocoa beans. It can be a liquid, solid, or paste. It is eaten on its own and used to flavor other foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg/330px-Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"},{"title":"Chocolate (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color chocolate or cocoa brown is a shade of brown that resembles chocolate. At right is displayed the color traditionally called chocolate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Chocolate02.jpg/330px-Chocolate02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Milky_Bar_Ad.jpg/500px-Milky_Bar_Ad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Milky_Bar_Ad.jpg/1280px-Milky_Bar_Ad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Milky_Bar_Ad.jpg/500px-Milky_Bar_Ad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1936 ad for Milkybar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMilky_Bar_Ad.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Norfolk_Pea_Tart_-_Benedicts.jpg/500px-Norfolk_Pea_Tart_-_Benedicts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Norfolk_Pea_Tart_-_Benedicts.jpg/500px-Norfolk_Pea_Tart_-_Benedicts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"White chocolate is featured in savory dishes, as seen above in a pea tart topped with caviar and white chocolate.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANorfolk_Pea_Tart_-_Benedicts.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/White_chocolate_and_macadamia_cookies.jpg/500px-White_chocolate_and_macadamia_cookies.jpg?u